doesn't contribute to any potential melds, and keeping it blocks development of cleaner patterns. Discarding it maintains my T4-T5-T6 chow, preserves flexibility in the Dot suit with three pairs (B1, B2, B8), and keeps the W1-W1-W2 structure which could develop into useful melds.\n\nAnswer: Play W6"}
